# SEO and vite-ssg

Full maintenance guide: **`docs/seo.md`**. Read it before adding routes, views, or marketing pages.

## New public page

- [ ] `useSeoMeta` in the view (`title`, `description`, `ogTitle`, `ogDescription`, `ogImage`, `twitterCard`; defaults from `src/lib/seo.ts`)
- [ ] Path in **`SSG_PUBLIC_PATHS`** (`src/lib/ssg-routes.ts`) — required for static HTML in `dist/`
- [ ] Path in **`publicPaths`** (`src/router/index.ts`) if reachable when signed in
- [ ] Rebuild; verify `dist/<path>.html` meta and body

## New dynamic route (`:slug`, `:id`, …)

- [ ] Implement fetch in **`fetchDynamicRoutePaths`** (`src/lib/ssg-routes.ts`); build must reach the data source
- [ ] `useSeoMeta` with **`computed()`** from page data

## Auth-only pages

- `useSeoMeta` optional; do **not** add to `SSG_PUBLIC_PATHS` unless intentionally indexable.

## Hard constraints

- **`@unhead/vue` v2** only (vite-ssg peer); do not upgrade to v3 without upgrading vite-ssg
- Set **`VITE_SITE_URL`** in deploy for absolute `og:image` at build time
- Browser-only setup/render → **`<ClientOnly>`** or SSR guards (`import.meta.env.SSR`)
